description:
Implement an `EventEmitter` class with `on(event, listener)`, `off(event, listener)`, and `emit(event, ...args)` methods.

**Example:**
```js
const emitter = new EventEmitter();
const handler = (msg) => console.log(msg);
emitter.on('greet', handler);
emitter.emit('greet', 'hello'); // logs 'hello'
emitter.off('greet', handler);
emitter.emit('greet', 'hello'); // nothing
```

